{
  "$comment": "Authoritative cases for the text projections an agent reads - `ui compact`, `ui tree`, `ui tree --semantics`, `ui regions` - read by BOTH the Kotlin (reticle-core RenderContractTest) and Swift (ReticleProtocol RenderContractTests) suites, so the Android helper and the iOS host cannot format one snapshot two ways. Each case is a snapshot plus, per view, the exact lines `Render` must produce. The renderers used to live in the Kotlin helper and in ReticleProtocol independently, pinned only by hand-mirrored unit tests - which is how `compact` drifted before; the derivations were shared while the formatting was not. What the cases pin beyond the line format: lost window focus outranks the keyboard line (nothing is tappable, however tappable it looks); the keyboard header counts what it covers; window grouping is topmost-first with the item lines left byte-for-byte unindented; nodes outside any window are announced rather than dropped; the fold footer states what a token-cheap view left out; every boundary marker renders rather than going silent; and both projections list nodes in document order, not in map order, so several roots print the same on either platform.",
